00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.840
The first theory that could explain the alleged&nbsp;
error Leonardo made in this painting comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:50.080
Isaacson himself. According to him, Leonardo&nbsp;
may have omitted the distortion deliberately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:56.560
for a theological reason. In a way, by bypassing&nbsp;
the natural laws of optics, Leonardo would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.920
showing the miraculous nature of Christ and&nbsp;
of the sphere he holds. Under this reading,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:07.600
the ones who would be mistaken would be us,&nbsp;
for interpreting the sphere as earthly crystal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:13.360
when in reality it should be interpreted as&nbsp;
heaven itself in his hands. And in that sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.360
it would make sense that heaven&nbsp;
does not obey the laws of physics.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:22.480
The second theory comes from Martin Kemp,&nbsp;
emeritus professor at Oxford and one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.560
the experts we have already cited in other&nbsp;
Leonardo analyses. Curiously, Kemp states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:34.080
that it was precisely the sphere that convinced&nbsp;
him the work was by Leonardo. According to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.520
the inclusions are painted exactly as they&nbsp;
appear in real rock crystal. And regarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:45.440
the lack of distortion, his explanation is&nbsp;
that Renaissance painting is not a photograph.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:51.840
Artists of the time considered it pictorial bad&nbsp;
taste to take optics to its final consequences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:57.120
As he himself said, it would not make sense to&nbsp;
imagine a baptism of Christ in which Jesus's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:03.040
legs appeared refracted by the water of the&nbsp;
Jordan River. That would not make sense either.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.560
But the third theory is perhaps&nbsp;
the most surprising of all.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:11.440
In 2019, a team of scientists from the&nbsp;
University of California, Irvine decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:16.960
to solve the mystery with modern technology,&nbsp;
creating a virtual three-dimensional model of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.920
the painting and simulating how light would&nbsp;
pass through different types of spheres.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.600
And in this study, something&nbsp;
quite unexpected was found.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:30.960
If the sphere were not solid, but hollow, like&nbsp;
a blown glass bubble with a thickness of barely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:36.240
one millimeter, the image it would produce&nbsp;
matches exactly what Leonardo painted in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:42.560
work. This way there would be no inversion,&nbsp;
no magnification, only minimal distortion.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.920
And there is one detail that makes this theory&nbsp;
even more convincing. Of the five folds of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:54.160
robe that pass behind the sphere, four appear&nbsp;
perfectly sharp. But one, right at the edge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.160 --> 00:07:00.160
appears deliberately blurred. Exactly where a&nbsp;
real hollow sphere would produce that distortion.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:05.680
So if we choose to believe this theory is the&nbsp;
correct one, Leonardo would not have made any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.800
mistake here. Quite the opposite. He would&nbsp;
have painted the sphere with such precision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:15.680
that it would have taken us five hundred&nbsp;
years to realize he was right all along.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.960
To this day, the sphere in this painting&nbsp;
continues to generate debates among physicists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:26.320
art historians, and scientists. Every new&nbsp;
technology applied to it reveals another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.320
layer of knowledge hidden within it.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:33.440
And perhaps that is the answer to the mystery.&nbsp;
That there is no error in this painting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.560
but rather that every decision, from the&nbsp;
microscopic inclusions to the blurred fold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.480
was made by someone who knew&nbsp;
exactly what he was doing.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:48.240
I would love for you to leave me in the comments&nbsp;
which of the theories you find most convincing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.920
and as always, thank you for&nbsp;
watching the video until the end.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:08:00.000
Thank you for your support, and&nbsp;
I will see you in the next video.

